{
  "_about": [
    "Community goals (Shared/community/CommunityData.cs reads this; the world server's CommunityGoals counts them; tools/wiki_community.py builds the wiki's Community Goals page from it).",
    "Each week (Monday 00:00 UTC) 'slots' goals are drawn from 'goals', one per 'group', the groups in turn so each comes back only after the others; 'weight' picks between a group's goals. The week's draw is kept in Redis when it starts, so changes here only change the weeks to come.",
    "A goal: 'event' what counts and 'filter' what narrows it (as in quests.json), 'goal' the whole server's target, 'minimum' what an account must add to share the rewards, 'icon' an object id the window shows. A kill, a dungeon cleared, a realm closed or an Arena wave counts once towards the total however many share it, and once for each of them.",
    "Tiers: reached at 'tierShares' of the goal and named 'tierNames'. Every account past the minimum claims each tier reached, from the Warcaller by the Nexus spawn; the top 'topCount' contributors claim the 'top' prize too once the goal ends. Past the goal, an Overdrive level ('bonusName') each 'bonusStep' of the goal more, up to 'bonusTiers', each paying the goal's 'bonus'. A goal without 'tiers', 'bonus' or 'top' gives 'defaultTiers', 'defaultBonus' and 'defaultTop'.",
    "Rewards: {\"fame\": n} to the account, {\"item\": \"<id>\", \"count\": n} to the gift chest in the vault, {\"roll\": n} n items drawn from the goal's 'loot' (by 'weight'; each Overdrive level makes the rarer 'rarities' likelier by 'rarityLift', and the top's prize rolls at the highest). A roll of 'announceFrom' or rarer is told to the whole server. Rewards stay claimable 'claimWeeks' weeks after a goal ends. Each goal gives its own (the server warns of two that give the same).",
    "Specials: goals with 'from' and 'until' (UTC days, yyyy-MM-dd, both included) run besides the week's. Give each a new id.",
    "Sizing: a week's run of a goal is its 'goal' times the goal's scale, fixed when the run begins. When it ends, the scale moves towards the realm ending at 'adapt.target' of the goal: times (done/target)^damping, between 'minStep' and 'maxStep' a run, and within 'minScale' and 'maxScale'. Specials are never scaled.",
    "Finishing early: a week's goal that reaches its last Overdrive level ends there, and a bonus goal of another group (none of this week's, and if it can, none of last week's or next week's) takes its slot until the weekly reset, as usual. Not with less than 'early.minHours' left. The faster it was finished, the harder things get: its pace over a whole week moves its goal's next run as 'adapt' does, up to 'early.maxStep' at once, and the bonus goal is that many times its usual size, times the heat of the run it replaced, up to 'early.maxHeat', so quick finishes in a row get harder each time until the weekly reset. A bonus run is sized again by its pace when it ends. 'early.enabled' false turns it off."
  ],
